cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill in your research or writing, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Humanities Writing Companion: An Agent Skill for Voice-Preserving Humanities Academic Writing"
version: 5.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Cong
    alias: tizzy916
    affiliation: "Tianyu Vision (TIANYU VISION); MA, History of Science, Tsinghua University"
    website: "https://tianyu.art/"
abstract: >
  An end-to-end agent skill, in the open Agent Skills (SKILL.md) format, for humanities
  scholars (history, philosophy, literature, cultural studies, art history,
  religious studies, classics, intellectual history, science studies, and
  adjacent fields) whose primary deliverable is a long-form argumentative
  text. Twelve work modes (A-L) cover the full writing lifecycle:
  research-question sharpening (Mode H Socratic), literature mapping
  (Mode I), plan-only outlining (Mode J), conception and drafting (Mode C),
  paragraph dialogue (Mode A), chapter review (Mode B four-layer critique),
  devil's advocate with 1-5 calibration and methodology-focus sub-mode
  (Mode D, with evidence-based concessions), writing-bottleneck assistance
  (Mode E), draft revision with
  revision-coach sub-mode (Mode F), context-aware promise-delivery checking
  (Mode G), factual AI-use disclosure with target-policy checks (Mode K), and defense/external-review
  comment integration via a revision-dossier workflow (Mode L). Deep-voice
  preservation ("my hand writes my voice"), discipline-specific critique
  routing on a three-layer architecture (6 L1 main disciplines with
  subfield inheritance, 9 L3 cross-disciplinary fields, 2 humanities-
  adjacent fields), ADHD-friendly interaction design, multi-agent parallel
  review fan-out in agent-capable environments, and engineering-grade
  infrastructure (version control, systematic validation, and a five-script
  toolchain requiring zsh and Python 3, with no third-party Python packages:
  stylistic clue scanning, pending-marker aggregation, citation-consistency
  checking, citation format conversion, and Crossref/OpenAlex metadata
  candidate lookup, not source-text or claim verification). Bilingual:
  SKILL.md, README, and references in
  English and Chinese.
